========================================================================
3. DE2.9 / SPRINT 2.9 honesty (not closed)
========================================================================

SPRINT “What got fixed” **DE2.9**:

> `ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret.oo:175-186` println walker →
> `c_secret_emit_guard(env, id, ...)`

Those lines (HEAD **and** WT) are:

```
if sid == "println" || sid == "eprintln" {
    … walk IDENT until RPAREN …
    c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved(env, sid, nm);
}
```

`c_secret_emit_guard` takes lowered C `a0/a1/a2/args`, **not** a token
index. The claimed call is a **type mismatch**; it was never landed.

WT dirt on `c_emit_secret*.oo` is **7.10** `str_slice` + **2.10**
`__sec_sink__` — not 2.9. `c_emit_print.oo` / `c_emit_ident.oo` match
HEAD. Host ELF **07:49** predates those hunks; println rails were
already in the ELF.

`eprintln` as a **stmt** is **not** special-cased → `c_emit_expr` →
`c_secret_emit_guard`. That is why eprintln “uses the walker” and
stmt println does not (s71_security R1).

